{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789263501,"nonce":"B8zDxNkmMcx9ekbTyoBwmghIryY=","title":"Symbol hash: HashLink's collision probe","message":"HashLink's hl_hash caches names and, when two live names collide, probes\nh+1 for the second. The core's symbol::hash returns the base hash from\nash's hlp_hash_gen (multiply by 223 per UTF-16 unit, remainder\n0x1FFFFF7B) with no probing. A name that collided inside an ash process\nwould therefore hash one higher there than here. Rare; decide whether\nthe core mirrors the probe (needs the same insertion order as ash's\ncache) or ash's adapter maps names to the core's symbols by string.","files":null}]}